\subsection{Convergence rate of MLE}
In this section, we aim to characterize the convergence rate of conditional MLE \eqref{eq:mle-est} in terms of the critical radius $\delta_{n,\Gcal}$ of function class $\Gcal$ and model misspecification. Specifically, we prove the following Theorem: 
\begin{theorem}[Convergence rate for misspecified MLE]\label{thm:mle-conv-rate}
    Suppose Assumption \ref{ass:lower-bound} and condition in Theorem \ref{thm: mle-nonmisspec-noniter} holds, and there exists $g^{\dagger} \in \Gcal$ such that $\E_{z\sim g_0}[\kl(g_0(\cdot|z), g^{\dag}(\cdot|z))] \leq \epsilon_\Gcal$. Then we have $$
    \E_{z\sim g(z)}\big[H^2(\hat{g}(\cdot|z)| g_0(\cdot|z))\big] \leq \delta_n^2 + \epsilon_{\Gcal}
    $$
    holds with probability at least $1- c_1\exp(c_2 \frac{c_0}{C+c_0}n\delta_n^2)$.
\end{theorem}
