 The critical radius $\delta_{n,\Fcal}$ of function class $\Fcal^*$ is any solution such that \begin{align*}
    \delta^2 \geq c/n \text{ and }\bar{R}_n (\delta; \Fcal^*)\leq \delta^2/b.
\end{align*}
Such critical radius can be easily calculated for a large number of function classes. For example, we can use $$
\frac{64}{\sqrt{n}}\int_{\delta^2/2b}^{\delta}\sqrt{\log N_n(t, \Bcal(\delta,\Fcal^*))}dt \leq \frac{\delta^2}{b}
